IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `rtad-drivers`

-- Road Traffic (Authorisation to Drive) Act 2008 (WA), with the Regulations 2014 and Road Traffic Code 2000 r 17 -- the
-- Q&A layer: the questions people ask, with the seat and the situation as parameters.
--
-- PURPOSE. One module whose exported questions serve every seat from one deployment. Every exported question takes
-- `my role` first ("Which of these describes you"). A question about another role answers `does not arise for you`
-- without reading any other input, so the site's question form never asks those inputs and drops the question.
--
-- ROLES. The Act and the regulations put duties on, and give standing to, two kinds of person who would ask them:
--   - the learner and the licensed driver: the baseline's seat (rtad-drivers.l4);
--   - the person who supervises a learner, or rides with a new driver: the r 43 instructor who must accompany the
--     learner (s 10(2), r 47(3)(a)), whose supervised hours go in the logbook (r 16A(2)(a), (b)), who may be "the person
--     in charge" who must see that L plates are displayed (r 49(3)), who may drive with L plates only while instructing
--     (r 49(4)), and who may be the "experienced driver" that lifts a new driver's passenger limit (r 11(3)(a), (4)).
-- The CEO of the Department of Transport, the police and the courts are never seats: their powers appear as what they
-- mean for the person asking. An employer or parent who gives the written document of r 11(3)(c) or r 22(3), (4) is not
-- a seat here (NOTES.md, "Q&A layer").
--
-- SITUATIONS (design D8 of the Graffiti Vandalism Act encoding). Within a role, a question that arises only in a
-- situation takes that situation's fact straight after `my role`, and answers `does not arise for you` when it does not
-- hold, without reading anything else. The questions of one situation share one input, with one name, type and @desc.
-- For the learner and driver:
--   - `I hold a learner's permit` (BOOLEAN): the permit's force, supervision, the drive it authorises, its speed limit
--     and its condition fine (s 10, r 42-48);
--   - `I hold a driver's licence` (BOOLEAN): novice type, provisional licence, P plates, the night-time and passenger
--     restrictions (s 40, r 4, 9, 10, 11, 36);
--   - `I have committed, or am said to have committed, a traffic offence` (BOOLEAN): points, modified penalty, when they
--     are recorded and expire, and whether a points notice follows (s 40(1A), 41, 43-50; r 65, 66; Code r 17);
--   - `I have been given a demerit points notice` (BOOLEAN): when the disqualification may start, and the s 51 election;
--   - `I have made a good behaviour election` (BOOLEAN): breaking it, and its doubled disqualification (s 51(3), 52);
--   - `I have been convicted of a driving offence, or disqualified` (BOOLEAN): what happens to the licence, the s 16(2)
--     period, s 18, s 23 and s 24.
-- For the supervisor: `I am the person in charge of the vehicle the learner drives` (BOOLEAN), for the two questions of
-- r 49(3). The questions of commencement (s 2, s 66), of getting a permit or licence (r 44-46, r 15, r 16A) and of
-- authorisation to drive at all (r 35(1)) arise in every situation of the driver's role, and the supervisor's other
-- questions in every situation of theirs, so they take no situation input.
--
-- The rules are in rtad-drivers.l4. This module calls them and restates none; where a supervisor's question needs a
-- rule the baseline does not export from that seat, a helper here builds it from the baseline's own functions. For the
-- learner and driver, where the situation holds, each answer is the baseline export's own, wrapped in a type that can
-- also say `does not arise for you`. No exported question takes a DEONTIC or EVENT input.
--
-- BASELINE. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md, "Q&A layer (seat and situations as parameters)".

§ `Road Traffic (Authorisation to Drive) Act 2008 (WA) -- the questions people ask`

§§ `Who is asking, and the shape of the answers`

DECLARE Role IS ONE OF
    `I am learning to drive, or hold a driver's licence`
    `I supervise a learner driver, or ride with a new driver`

DECLARE `Yes or no` IS ONE OF
    yes
    no
    `does not arise for you`

DECLARE `Penalty units` IS ONE OF
    `does not arise for you`
    `penalty units` HAS `the number of penalty units` IS A NUMBER

DECLARE `Demerit points` IS ONE OF
    `does not arise for you`
    `demerit points` HAS `the number of points` IS A NUMBER

DECLARE `Months` IS ONE OF
    `does not arise for you`
    `for months` HAS `the number of months` IS A NUMBER

DECLARE `Speed` IS ONE OF
    `does not arise for you`
    `km/h` HAS `the speed in km/h` IS A NUMBER

DECLARE `Date answer` IS ONE OF
    `does not arise for you`
    `on or after` HAS `the earliest day` IS A DATE

DECLARE `Permit answer` IS ONE OF
    `does not arise for you`
    `the permit answer` HAS `what the Act says of my permit` IS A `Learner's permit answer`

DECLARE `Novice answer` IS ONE OF
    `does not arise for you`
    `I am a` HAS `my novice status` IS A `Novice status`

DECLARE `Plates answer` IS ONE OF
    `does not arise for you`
    `I must display` HAS `the plates` IS A `P plates`

DECLARE `Licence answer` IS ONE OF
    `does not arise for you`
    `my licence or permit is` HAS `what happens to it` IS A `What happens to my licence`

-- The supervisor's standing (s 10(2), r 43(2)), in the supervisor's own words. Read only through the helper below, which
-- lists every value and has no OTHERWISE (graffiti finding 31).
DECLARE `My standing to supervise` IS ONE OF
    `I hold a driving instructor's licence (Motor Vehicle Drivers Instructors Act 1963)`
    `I am an instructor in a youth driver education course run or supervised by a body the CEO authorised`
    `I hold an Australian driver licence or a foreign driving authorisation for this kind of driving`
    `I hold only a learner's permit for it, or no licence for it`

§§ `Building the baseline's inputs`

GIVEN `it holds` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`yes if` `it holds` MEANS
    IF `it holds` THEN yes ELSE no

GIVEN `my standing` IS A `My standing to supervise`
GIVETH A Supervisor
`the supervisor I am` `my standing` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my standing`
    WHEN `I hold a driving instructor's licence (Motor Vehicle Drivers Instructors Act 1963)` THEN `a licensed driving instructor`
    WHEN `I am an instructor in a youth driver education course run or supervised by a body the CEO authorised` THEN `a youth driver education course instructor`
    WHEN `I hold an Australian driver licence or a foreign driving authorisation for this kind of driving` THEN `another licensed driver`
    WHEN `I hold only a learner's permit for it, or no licence for it` THEN `nobody qualified`

-- r 49(4)(b): the driver "is authorised to give, and is driving in the course of giving, driving instruction to the
-- learner", with the learner "sitting beside the driver". Authorised to give instruction: s 10(2) and r 43(2), the
-- baseline's own test.
GIVEN `my standing` IS A `My standing to supervise`
      `years I have held a licence for this kind of driving` IS A NUMBER
      `the learner is learning to ride a moped` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the learner is sitting beside me` IS A BOOLEAN
      `I am driving in the course of instructing the learner` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `r 49(4)(b) -- I may drive with L plates while instructing the learner beside me` IF
        `May this person supervise me` (`the supervisor I am` `my standing`) `years I have held a licence for this kind of driving` `the learner is learning to ride a moped`
    AND `the learner is sitting beside me`
    AND `I am driving in the course of instructing the learner`

§§ `For the learner and the licensed driver`

§§§ `ss 2, 66 -- does this Act govern me`

@export Does the Road Traffic (Authorisation to Drive) Act 2008 govern my permit or licence on this day (s 2)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `the day` IS A DATE @desc The day the question is about
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Does this Act govern my permit or licence on this day` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am learning to drive, or hold a driver's licence` THEN `yes if` (`Does this Act govern my authorisation to drive on` `the day`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export Is my learner's permit from before 27 April 2015 now taken to be a learner's permit under this Act (s 66)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `issued under the Road Traffic Act 1974 section 43(1)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your permit was issued under the Road Traffic Act 1974 s 43(1)
      `in effect immediately before 27 April 2015` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether it was still in effect the day before the Act began
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Is my permit from before 27 April 2015 taken to be a learner's permit under this Act` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am learning to drive, or hold a driver's licence` THEN `yes if` (`Is my old permit taken to be a learner's permit under this Act` `issued under the Road Traffic Act 1974 section 43(1)` `in effect immediately before 27 April 2015`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

§§§ `s 10, s 11A; r 44-46 -- getting a learner's permit`

@export Am I old enough to hold a learner's permit (Regulations r 44)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `my date of birth` IS A DATE @desc Your date of birth
      `the day` IS A DATE @desc The day the question is about
      `for a moped only` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the permit is to learn to ride only a moped
      `the CEO waived the age for undue hardship` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the CEO has waived the minimum age because refusing would cause you undue hardship
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Am I old enough for a learner's permit` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am learning to drive, or hold a driver's licence` THEN `yes if` (`Am I old enough to hold a learner's permit` `my date of birth` `the day` `for a moped only` `the CEO waived the age for undue hardship`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export Can I be issued a learner's permit (s 10, s 11A; Regulations r 44 to r 46)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `old enough` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you meet the minimum age (see the learner's permit age question)
      `passed the theory test or had it waived` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have shown the CEO knowledge of the traffic laws and safe driving, or the CEO waived it
      `hold any prerequisite licence Schedule 8 requires` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you hold the licence Schedule 8 requires for this class (nothing is required for a car or a moped)
      `gave identity, WA address, photograph and signature` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have given proof of identity and WA address, and a photograph and signature
GIVETH A `Permit answer`
`Can I get a learner's permit` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am learning to drive, or hold a driver's licence` THEN `the permit answer` (`Can I be issued a learner's permit` `old enough` `passed the theory test or had it waived` `hold any prerequisite licence Schedule 8 requires` `gave identity, WA address, photograph and signature`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

§§§ `s 10(2), (4); r 42, 43, 47, 48 -- driving on my learner's permit`

@export Is my learner's permit in force on this day (s 10(4); Regulations r 42(3), r 53)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `I hold a learner's permit` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you hold a learner's permit (or held one, if the question is whether it is still in force)
      `the day it was issued` IS A DATE @desc The day your learner's permit was issued
      `the day` IS A DATE @desc The day the question is about
      `cancelled or suspended by the CEO` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the CEO has cancelled or suspended it by written notice
      `granted a licence for the driving I was learning` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have since been granted a driver's licence for that kind of driving
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Is my learner's permit in force on this day` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am learning to drive, or hold a driver's licence` THEN
        IF NOT `I hold a learner's permit`
        THEN `does not arise for you`
        ELSE `yes if` (`Is my learner's permit in force` `the day it was issued` `the day` `cancelled or suspended by the CEO` `granted a licence for the driving I was learning`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export May this person supervise my driving on a learner's permit (s 10(2); Regulations r 43)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `I hold a learner's permit` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you hold a learner's permit (or held one, if the question is whether it is still in force)
      `the supervisor` IS A Supervisor @desc Who is supervising you
      `years held` IS A NUMBER @desc For another licensed driver: years they have held a licence for the kind of driving you are learning
      `learning a moped` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are learning to ride a moped
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`May this person supervise my driving` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am learning to drive, or hold a driver's licence` THEN
        IF NOT `I hold a learner's permit`
        THEN `does not arise for you`
        ELSE `yes if` (`May this person supervise me` `the supervisor` `years held` `learning a moped`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export Does my learner's permit authorise this drive (s 10; Regulations r 42, r 47, r 48(1))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `I hold a learner's permit` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you hold a learner's permit (or held one, if the question is whether it is still in force)
      `the drive` IS A `My learning drive` @desc The drive you are asking about
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Does my learner's permit authorise this drive of mine` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am learning to drive, or hold a driver's licence` THEN
        IF NOT `I hold a learner's permit`
        THEN `does not arise for you`
        ELSE `yes if` (`Does my learner's permit authorise this drive` `the drive`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export What is the fastest I may drive on a learner's permit (Regulations r 47(3)(b))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `I hold a learner's permit` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you hold a learner's permit (or held one, if the question is whether it is still in force)
GIVETH A `Speed`
`What is the fastest I may drive on a learner's permit` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am learning to drive, or hold a driver's licence` THEN
        IF NOT `I hold a learner's permit`
        THEN `does not arise for you`
        ELSE `km/h` `What is the fastest I may drive on my learner's permit`
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export What is the most I can be fined for breaking a learner's permit condition (Regulations r 48(2))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `I hold a learner's permit` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you hold a learner's permit (or held one, if the question is whether it is still in force)
GIVETH A `Penalty units`
`What is the most I can be fined for breaking a learner's permit condition` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am learning to drive, or hold a driver's licence` THEN
        IF NOT `I hold a learner's permit`
        THEN `does not arise for you`
        ELSE `penalty units` `What is the most I can be fined for breaking a learner's condition`
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

§§§ `r 15, 22, 16A -- getting a driver's licence`

@export Am I old enough to hold a driver's licence (Regulations r 15, r 22(2) to (4))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `my date of birth` IS A DATE @desc Your date of birth
      `the day` IS A DATE @desc The day the question is about
      `a moped licence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the licence is a moped licence
      `the CEO waived the age for undue hardship` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the CEO has waived the minimum age because refusing would cause you undue hardship
      `the written consent or employer confirmation r 22 requires was given` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a parent (or, if none lives in WA, a parent or employer) gave the written consent or confirmation r 22 requires
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Am I old enough for a driver's licence` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am learning to drive, or hold a driver's licence` THEN `yes if` (`Am I old enough to hold a driver's licence` `my date of birth` `the day` `a moped licence` `the CEO waived the age for undue hardship` `the written consent or employer confirmation r 22 requires was given`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export Have I shown I can drive safely, as a new applicant under 25 for a car licence (Regulations r 16A)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `my experience` IS A `My driving experience` @desc Your logbook hours and test results
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Have I shown I can drive safely, as a new applicant under 25` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am learning to drive, or hold a driver's licence` THEN `yes if` (`Have I shown I can drive safely for a car licence` `my experience`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

§§§ `s 40; r 4, 9, 10, 11, 36 -- my licence while I am new to it`

@export What kind of novice driver am I (s 40(2), (3); Regulations r 4)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `I hold a driver's licence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you hold a driver's licence (a provisional licence counts; a learner's permit does not)
      `months held` IS A NUMBER @desc Months you have held a driver's licence (not a learner's permit), not counting months you were excluded by law from driving
GIVETH A `Novice answer`
`What kind of novice driver am I now` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am learning to drive, or hold a driver's licence` THEN
        IF NOT `I hold a driver's licence`
        THEN `does not arise for you`
        ELSE `I am a` (`What kind of novice driver am I` `months held`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export Must my licence be (or stay) provisional (Regulations r 9)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `I hold a driver's licence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you hold a driver's licence (a provisional licence counts; a learner's permit does not)
      `my date of birth` IS A DATE @desc Your date of birth
      `the day` IS A DATE @desc The day the question is about
      `months held` IS A NUMBER @desc Months you have held a driver's licence (not a learner's permit), not counting months you were excluded by law from driving
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Must my licence be or stay provisional` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am learning to drive, or hold a driver's licence` THEN
        IF NOT `I hold a driver's licence`
        THEN `does not arise for you`
        ELSE `yes if` (`Must my licence be provisional` `my date of birth` `the day` `months held`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export What P plates must I display (Regulations r 36)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `I hold a driver's licence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you hold a driver's licence (a provisional licence counts; a learner's permit does not)
      `provisional` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your licence is a provisional licence
      `months held` IS A NUMBER @desc Months you have held a driver's licence (not a learner's permit), not counting months you were excluded by law from driving
GIVETH A `Plates answer`
`What P plates must I display on my car` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am learning to drive, or hold a driver's licence` THEN
        IF NOT `I hold a driver's licence`
        THEN `does not arise for you`
        ELSE `I must display` (`What P plates must I display` `provisional` `months held`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export May I drive between midnight and 5 a.m. (Regulations r 10, r 57)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `I hold a driver's licence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you hold a driver's licence (a provisional licence counts; a learner's permit does not)
      `months held` IS A NUMBER @desc Months you have held a driver's licence (not a learner's permit), not counting months you were excluded by law from driving
      `the purpose` IS A `Night purpose` @desc Why you are driving
      `the CEO gave me a written permit` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the CEO has given you a written permit to drive (r 57)
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`May I drive between midnight and 5 a.m.` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am learning to drive, or hold a driver's licence` THEN
        IF NOT `I hold a driver's licence`
        THEN `does not arise for you`
        ELSE `yes if` (`May I drive between midnight and 5 am` `months held` `the purpose` `the CEO gave me a written permit`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export May I carry these passengers (Regulations r 11, r 94)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `I hold a driver's licence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you hold a driver's licence (a provisional licence counts; a learner's permit does not)
      `the day` IS A DATE @desc The day the question is about
      `months held` IS A NUMBER @desc Months you have held a driver's licence (not a learner's permit), not counting months you were excluded by law from driving
      `the passengers` IS A `My passengers` @desc Who is in the car with you
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`May I carry these passengers in my car` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am learning to drive, or hold a driver's licence` THEN
        IF NOT `I hold a driver's licence`
        THEN `does not arise for you`
        ELSE `yes if` (`May I carry these passengers` `the day` `months held` `the passengers`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

§§§ `r 35(1), 48(1), 55, 57 -- am I authorised to drive at all`

@export Am I authorised to drive this vehicle on this drive (Regulations r 35(1), r 48(1), r 55, r 57; s 23)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `my drive` IS A `My drive` @desc Your licence and the drive you are asking about
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Am I authorised to drive this vehicle on this drive` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am learning to drive, or hold a driver's licence` THEN `yes if` (`Am I authorised to drive` `my drive`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

§§§ `s 16, 17, 18, 23, 24; r 53B, 53C -- when I am convicted or disqualified`

@export Does a licence or permit I obtain while disqualified have any effect (s 23)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `I have been convicted of a driving offence, or disqualified` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have been convicted of a driving offence, or disqualified from holding or obtaining a driver's licence (by a court, by demerit points or by a fines enforcement order)
      `disqualified when I obtained it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you were disqualified from holding or obtaining a licence when it was obtained
      `an extraordinary licence ordered by a court` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether it is an extraordinary licence granted on a court's order
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Does a licence or permit I obtain while disqualified have any effect` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am learning to drive, or hold a driver's licence` THEN
        IF NOT `I have been convicted of a driving offence, or disqualified`
        THEN `does not arise for you`
        ELSE `yes if` (`Does a licence I obtain while disqualified have effect` `disqualified when I obtained it` `an extraordinary licence ordered by a court`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export What happens to my licence or learner's permit when I am disqualified (s 16, s 17; Regulations r 53B, r 53C)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `I have been convicted of a driving offence, or disqualified` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have been convicted of a driving offence, or disqualified from holding or obtaining a driver's licence (by a court, by demerit points or by a fines enforcement order)
      `provisional` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your licence is a provisional licence
      `how` IS A `How I am disqualified` @desc How you came to be disqualified, or convicted
      `an alcohol interlock offence or a repeat prescribed offence under r 53B` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For a court disqualification of a full licence or permit: whether the offence is an alcohol interlock offence or a repeat prescribed drink- or drug-driving offence
GIVETH A `Licence answer`
`What happens to my licence or permit when I am disqualified` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am learning to drive, or hold a driver's licence` THEN
        IF NOT `I have been convicted of a driving offence, or disqualified`
        THEN `does not arise for you`
        ELSE `my licence or permit is` (`What happens to my licence when I am disqualified` `provisional` `how` `an alcohol interlock offence or a repeat prescribed offence under r 53B`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export For how many months am I disqualified after my provisional licence is cancelled on conviction (s 16(2), s 18(3))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `I have been convicted of a driving offence, or disqualified` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have been convicted of a driving offence, or disqualified from holding or obtaining a driver's licence (by a court, by demerit points or by a fines enforcement order)
      `months disqualified by the court` IS A NUMBER @desc Months the court disqualified you for (0 if none)
GIVETH A `Months`
`For how many months am I disqualified after losing my provisional licence on conviction` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am learning to drive, or hold a driver's licence` THEN
        IF NOT `I have been convicted of a driving offence, or disqualified`
        THEN `does not arise for you`
        ELSE `for months` (`How many months am I disqualified after losing my provisional licence` `months disqualified by the court`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export Am I disqualified, as someone without a licence who would get a provisional one (s 18)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `I have been convicted of a driving offence, or disqualified` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have been convicted of a driving offence, or disqualified from holding or obtaining a driver's licence (by a court, by demerit points or by a fines enforcement order)
      `I hold a driver's licence now` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you hold a driver's licence (a learner's permit is not one)
      `my licence would have to be provisional` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a licence granted to you would have to be provisional (a novice, or under 19)
      `the conviction` IS A `What I was convicted of` @desc What you were convicted of
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Am I disqualified, as someone unlicensed who would get a provisional licence` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am learning to drive, or hold a driver's licence` THEN
        IF NOT `I have been convicted of a driving offence, or disqualified`
        THEN `does not arise for you`
        ELSE `yes if` (`Am I disqualified as an unlicensed would-be provisional driver` `I hold a driver's licence now` `my licence would have to be provisional` `the conviction`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export How many months must pass before I may apply to remove my court disqualification (s 24)? (0 means I cannot apply)
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `I have been convicted of a driving offence, or disqualified` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have been convicted of a driving offence, or disqualified from holding or obtaining a driver's licence (by a court, by demerit points or by a fines enforcement order)
      `months of disqualification` IS A NUMBER @desc The length of the court's disqualification, in months
      `permanent` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are disqualified permanently
GIVETH A `Months`
`How many months must pass before I may apply to remove my court disqualification` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am learning to drive, or hold a driver's licence` THEN
        IF NOT `I have been convicted of a driving offence, or disqualified`
        THEN `does not arise for you`
        ELSE `for months` (`How many months before I may apply to remove my disqualification` `months of disqualification` `permanent`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

§§§ `s 40(1A), 41, 43-50; r 65, 66; Code r 17 -- my offence and its demerit points`

@export How many demerit points does my speeding carry (Road Traffic Code 2000 r 17; Regulations r 65(3))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `I have committed, or am said to have committed, a traffic offence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have committed, or are said to have committed, a speeding or other road traffic offence
      `km/h over the limit` IS A NUMBER @desc How many km/h over the speed limit you were
      `in a holiday period` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the offence was in a holiday period (long weekend, Easter, Christmas)
      `on a motorised scooter or electric rideable device` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you were riding a motorised scooter or an electric rideable device
GIVETH A `Demerit points`
`How many demerit points does my speeding offence carry` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am learning to drive, or hold a driver's licence` THEN
        IF NOT `I have committed, or am said to have committed, a traffic offence`
        THEN `does not arise for you`
        ELSE `demerit points` (`How many demerit points does my speeding carry` `km/h over the limit` `in a holiday period` `on a motorised scooter or electric rideable device`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export What is the modified penalty for my speeding (Road Traffic Code 2000 r 17)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `I have committed, or am said to have committed, a traffic offence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have committed, or are said to have committed, a speeding or other road traffic offence
      `km/h over the limit` IS A NUMBER @desc How many km/h over the speed limit you were
      `driving a heavy vehicle` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you were driving a heavy vehicle
GIVETH A `Penalty units`
`What is the modified penalty for my speeding offence` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am learning to drive, or hold a driver's licence` THEN
        IF NOT `I have committed, or am said to have committed, a traffic offence`
        THEN `does not arise for you`
        ELSE `penalty units` (`What is the modified penalty for my speeding` `km/h over the limit` `driving a heavy vehicle`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export How many demerit points does this Road Traffic Act offence carry (Regulations r 65(2), r 66)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `I have committed, or am said to have committed, a traffic offence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have committed, or are said to have committed, a speeding or other road traffic offence
      `the offence` IS A `Road Traffic Act offence` @desc The offence
      `in a holiday period` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the offence was in a holiday period (long weekend, Easter, Christmas)
GIVETH A `Demerit points`
`How many demerit points does my Road Traffic Act offence carry` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am learning to drive, or hold a driver's licence` THEN
        IF NOT `I have committed, or am said to have committed, a traffic offence`
        THEN `does not arise for you`
        ELSE `demerit points` (`How many demerit points does this offence carry` `the offence` `in a holiday period`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export Has my infringement notice been "dealt with", so that points follow (s 40(1A), (1B))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `I have committed, or am said to have committed, a traffic offence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have committed, or are said to have committed, a speeding or other road traffic offence
      `the Fines Enforcement Act Part 3 applies` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Fines, Penalties and Infringement Notices Enforcement Act 1994 Part 3 applies to the notice (it does to a WA traffic infringement)
      `I paid something, even if the payment was dishonoured` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether any amount has been paid, even part, even if dishonoured
      `an order to pay or elect has been issued` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether an order to pay or elect has been issued to you
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Has my infringement notice been dealt with` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am learning to drive, or hold a driver's licence` THEN
        IF NOT `I have committed, or am said to have committed, a traffic offence`
        THEN `does not arise for you`
        ELSE `yes if` (`Am I dealt with by infringement notice` `the Fines Enforcement Act Part 3 applies` `I paid something, even if the payment was dishonoured` `an order to pay or elect has been issued`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export Is WA my demerit point registry jurisdiction (s 43)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `I have committed, or am said to have committed, a traffic offence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have committed, or are said to have committed, a speeding or other road traffic offence
      `I hold a WA licence or learner's permit` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you hold a WA driver's licence or learner's permit
      `I hold another jurisdiction's authorisation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you hold an interstate licence or permit
      `I held one before` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If you hold neither: whether you held one before
      `the most recent was from WA` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If so: whether the most recent was a WA one
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Is WA my registry jurisdiction for demerit points` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am learning to drive, or hold a driver's licence` THEN
        IF NOT `I have committed, or am said to have committed, a traffic offence`
        THEN `does not arise for you`
        ELSE `yes if` (`Is WA my demerit point registry jurisdiction` `I hold a WA licence or learner's permit` `I hold another jurisdiction's authorisation` `I held one before` `the most recent was from WA`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export Will demerit points be recorded against me (s 44 to s 47)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `I have committed, or am said to have committed, a traffic offence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have committed, or are said to have committed, a speeding or other road traffic offence
      `I am an individual` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are an individual (not a company)
      `a demerit point offence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the offence carries demerit points
      `an offence under a WA road law` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether it is an offence under WA law (not interstate)
      `WA is my registry jurisdiction` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether WA is your demerit point registry jurisdiction
      `the outcome` IS A `How my offence ended` @desc How the offence has been dealt with
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Will demerit points be recorded against me for this offence` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am learning to drive, or hold a driver's licence` THEN
        IF NOT `I have committed, or am said to have committed, a traffic offence`
        THEN `does not arise for you`
        ELSE `yes if` (`Will demerit points be recorded against me` `I am an individual` `a demerit point offence` `an offence under a WA road law` `WA is my registry jurisdiction` `the outcome`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export Are the demerit points for this offence still current on this day (s 48)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `I have committed, or am said to have committed, a traffic offence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have committed, or are said to have committed, a speeding or other road traffic offence
      `the day of the offence` IS A DATE @desc The day the offence was committed
      `the day` IS A DATE @desc The day the question is about
      `cancelled` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the points have been cancelled (for example by a notice under s 49 or s 50)
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Are the demerit points for this offence still current` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am learning to drive, or hold a driver's licence` THEN
        IF NOT `I have committed, or am said to have committed, a traffic offence`
        THEN `does not arise for you`
        ELSE `yes if` (`Are these demerit points current` `the day of the offence` `the day` `cancelled`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export For how many months will an excessive demerit points notice disqualify me (s 49)? (0 means no notice is due)
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `I have committed, or am said to have committed, a traffic offence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have committed, or are said to have committed, a speeding or other road traffic offence
      `my current demerit points` IS A NUMBER @desc Your current (unexpired, uncancelled) demerit points
GIVETH A `Months`
`For how many months will an excessive demerit points notice disqualify me` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am learning to drive, or hold a driver's licence` THEN
        IF NOT `I have committed, or am said to have committed, a traffic offence`
        THEN `does not arise for you`
        ELSE `for months` (`How many months does an excessive demerit points notice disqualify me` `my current demerit points`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export Must I be given an excessive demerit points (novice driver) notice, with 3 months' disqualification (s 50)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `I have committed, or am said to have committed, a traffic offence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have committed, or are said to have committed, a speeding or other road traffic offence
      `my current points after the offence` IS A NUMBER @desc Your current demerit points, counting this offence
      `months held when I offended` IS A NUMBER @desc Months you had held a licence (not counting excluded time) on the day of the offence
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Must I be given a novice driver notice for my points` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am learning to drive, or hold a driver's licence` THEN
        IF NOT `I have committed, or am said to have committed, a traffic offence`
        THEN `does not arise for you`
        ELSE `yes if` (`Must I be given a novice driver notice` `my current points after the offence` `months held when I offended`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

§§§ `s 49(2), 50(2)(d), 51, 52 -- after a demerit points notice`

@export What is the earliest day my demerit points disqualification can start (s 49(2), s 50(2)(d))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `I have been given a demerit points notice` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the CEO has given you an excessive demerit points notice (s 49) or an excessive demerit points (novice driver) notice (s 50)
      `the day the notice was given` IS A DATE @desc The day the CEO gave you the notice
      `a novice driver notice` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether it is a novice driver notice (s 50) rather than an excessive demerit points notice (s 49)
GIVETH A `Date answer`
`What is the earliest day my demerit points disqualification can start` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am learning to drive, or hold a driver's licence` THEN
        IF NOT `I have been given a demerit points notice`
        THEN `does not arise for you`
        ELSE `on or after` (`The earliest day my demerit disqualification can start` `the day the notice was given` `a novice driver notice`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export May I avoid the disqualification by electing a good behaviour year (s 51)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `I have been given a demerit points notice` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the CEO has given you an excessive demerit points notice (s 49) or an excessive demerit points (novice driver) notice (s 50)
      `I hold a driver's licence now` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you hold a driver's licence (a learner's permit is not one)
      `it is provisional` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether it is a provisional licence
      `months held` IS A NUMBER @desc Months you have held a driver's licence (not a learner's permit), not counting months you were excluded by law from driving
      `days since the notice was given` IS A NUMBER @desc Days since the CEO gave you the excessive demerit points notice
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`May I elect a good behaviour year instead of being disqualified` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am learning to drive, or hold a driver's licence` THEN
        IF NOT `I have been given a demerit points notice`
        THEN `does not arise for you`
        ELSE `yes if` (`May I make a section 51 election` `I hold a driver's licence now` `it is provisional` `months held` `days since the notice was given`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export Have I broken my good behaviour election (s 51(3), s 52(1))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `I have made a good behaviour election` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have made a good behaviour election under s 51
      `points recorded for offences in the election year` IS A NUMBER @desc Demerit points recorded for offences committed during the election year
      `convicted of an offence with mandatory or automatic disqualification` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you were convicted of an offence in that year for which disqualification is mandatory or automatic
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Have I broken my good behaviour election` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am learning to drive, or hold a driver's licence` THEN
        IF NOT `I have made a good behaviour election`
        THEN `does not arise for you`
        ELSE `yes if` (`Have I broken my election` `points recorded for offences in the election year` `convicted of an offence with mandatory or automatic disqualification`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export For how many months am I disqualified after breaking my election (s 52(4))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `I have made a good behaviour election` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have made a good behaviour election under s 51
      `months in the excessive demerit points notice` IS A NUMBER @desc The period stated in the original notice, in months
GIVETH A `Months`
`For how many months am I disqualified after breaking my good behaviour election` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am learning to drive, or hold a driver's licence` THEN
        IF NOT `I have made a good behaviour election`
        THEN `does not arise for you`
        ELSE `for months` (`How many months am I disqualified after breaking my election` `months in the excessive demerit points notice`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

§§ `For the person who supervises a learner driver, or rides with a new driver`

§§§ `s 10(2); r 43, 47, 16A -- supervising a learner`

@export May I supervise this learner's driving (s 10(2); Regulations r 43)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `my standing` IS A `My standing to supervise` @desc What you hold: a driving instructor's licence; an instructor's place in a youth driver education course the CEO authorised; an Australian driver licence or foreign driving authorisation for the kind of driving the learner is learning (a provisional licence counts); or only a learner's permit, or nothing, for it
      `years I have held a licence for this kind of driving` IS A NUMBER @desc For a licensed driver: years (adding up separate periods) you have held a licence for the kind of driving the learner is learning
      `the learner is learning to ride a moped` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the learner is learning to ride a moped
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`May I supervise this learner` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I supervise a learner driver, or ride with a new driver` THEN `yes if` (`May this person supervise me` (`the supervisor I am` `my standing`) `years I have held a licence for this kind of driving` `the learner is learning to ride a moped`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

-- s 10(2), r 47(3)(a), r 48(1): the learner is authorised only while accompanied by the instructor. The baseline's own
-- test, `Does my learner's permit authorise this drive`, is run with the supervisor's facts.
@export Is the learner authorised to drive on this drive, with me as the supervisor (s 10; Regulations r 42, r 43, r 47(3)(a), r 48(1))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `the learner's permit is in force` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the learner's permit is in force (not expired, cancelled or suspended)
      `the learner is driving solely to learn` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the learner is driving solely to learn to drive the vehicle
      `my standing` IS A `My standing to supervise` @desc What you hold: a driving instructor's licence; an instructor's place in a youth driver education course the CEO authorised; an Australian driver licence or foreign driving authorisation for the kind of driving the learner is learning (a provisional licence counts); or only a learner's permit, or nothing, for it
      `years I have held a licence for this kind of driving` IS A NUMBER @desc For a licensed driver: years (adding up separate periods) you have held a licence for the kind of driving the learner is learning
      `the learner is learning to ride a moped` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the learner is learning to ride a moped
      `I accompany the learner` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are with the learner for the whole of the drive
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Is the learner authorised to drive with me as the supervisor` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I supervise a learner driver, or ride with a new driver` THEN `yes if` (`Does my learner's permit authorise this drive` (`My learning drive` `the learner's permit is in force` `the learner is driving solely to learn` (`the supervisor I am` `my standing`) `years I have held a licence for this kind of driving` `the learner is learning to ride a moped` `I accompany the learner`))
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export What is the fastest the learner I supervise may drive (Regulations r 47(3)(b))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
GIVETH A `Speed`
`What is the fastest the learner I supervise may drive` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I supervise a learner driver, or ride with a new driver` THEN `km/h` `What is the fastest I may drive on my learner's permit`
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

-- r 16A(2)(a), (b): the hours count if driven "in the course of instruction by" a licensed driving instructor or "a
-- person who may give driving instruction under regulation 43(2)", and recorded in a logbook approved by the CEO,
-- "signed by the person who gave the instruction". r 16A is for a car licence (and a restricted motor cycle licence),
-- so the moped rule of r 43(2)(b)(i) is not read here: the 4-year rule applies.
@export Do the hours I supervise count towards the 50 logbook hours a learner under 25 needs for a car licence (Regulations r 16A(2)(a), (b))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `my standing` IS A `My standing to supervise` @desc What you hold: a driving instructor's licence; an instructor's place in a youth driver education course the CEO authorised; an Australian driver licence or foreign driving authorisation for the kind of driving the learner is learning (a provisional licence counts); or only a learner's permit, or nothing, for it
      `years I have held a licence for this kind of driving` IS A NUMBER @desc For a licensed driver: years (adding up separate periods) you have held a licence for the kind of driving the learner is learning
      `I sign the record of each drive in the CEO-approved logbook` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you sign the record of each drive you supervise in the logbook approved by the CEO
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Do the hours I supervise count towards the learner's logbook hours` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I supervise a learner driver, or ride with a new driver` THEN
        `yes if` (    `May this person supervise me` (`the supervisor I am` `my standing`) `years I have held a licence for this kind of driving` FALSE
                  AND `I sign the record of each drive in the CEO-approved logbook`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

§§§ `r 49 -- L plates`

@export Must I make sure L plates are displayed on the vehicle the learner drives (Regulations r 49(1), (3))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `I am the person in charge of the vehicle the learner drives` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are the person in charge of the vehicle the learner drives on a road
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Must I make sure L plates are displayed` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    -- r 49(3): "The person in charge of a motor vehicle that another person drives on a road while learning to drive must
    -- ensure that L plates are displayed as required by subregulation (1)." Asked of that person, so the answer is yes by
    -- the question's own terms.
    WHEN `I supervise a learner driver, or ride with a new driver` THEN
        IF NOT `I am the person in charge of the vehicle the learner drives`
        THEN `does not arise for you`
        ELSE yes
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export What is the most I can be fined if the L plates are not displayed (Regulations r 49(3))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `I am the person in charge of the vehicle the learner drives` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are the person in charge of the vehicle the learner drives on a road
GIVETH A `Penalty units`
`What is the most I can be fined if the L plates are not displayed` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    -- r 49(3): "Penalty for this subregulation: a fine of 2 PU. Modified penalty for this subregulation: 1 PU."
    WHEN `I supervise a learner driver, or ride with a new driver` THEN
        IF NOT `I am the person in charge of the vehicle the learner drives`
        THEN `does not arise for you`
        ELSE `penalty units` 2
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

-- r 49(4): "A person must not drive on a road a motor vehicle displaying an L plate unless -- (a) the person is driving
-- while learning ...; or (b) a person who is authorised as described in paragraph (a) (the learner) is sitting beside the
-- driver and the driver is authorised to give, and is driving in the course of giving, driving instruction to the
-- learner. Penalty for this subregulation: a fine of 2 PU." Asked of the supervisor, who is not driving while learning.
@export May I drive the vehicle while it displays L plates (Regulations r 49(4))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `my standing` IS A `My standing to supervise` @desc What you hold: a driving instructor's licence; an instructor's place in a youth driver education course the CEO authorised; an Australian driver licence or foreign driving authorisation for the kind of driving the learner is learning (a provisional licence counts); or only a learner's permit, or nothing, for it
      `years I have held a licence for this kind of driving` IS A NUMBER @desc For a licensed driver: years (adding up separate periods) you have held a licence for the kind of driving the learner is learning
      `the learner is learning to ride a moped` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the learner is learning to ride a moped
      `the learner is sitting beside me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the learner is sitting beside you while you drive
      `I am driving in the course of instructing the learner` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are driving in the course of giving the learner driving instruction (for example, showing how it is done)
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`May I drive the vehicle while it displays L plates` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I supervise a learner driver, or ride with a new driver` THEN `yes if` (`r 49(4)(b) -- I may drive with L plates while instructing the learner beside me` `my standing` `years I have held a licence for this kind of driving` `the learner is learning to ride a moped` `the learner is sitting beside me` `I am driving in the course of instructing the learner`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

§§§ `r 11(3)(a), (4) -- riding with a new driver`

-- r 11(3)(a), (4): a type 1A novice may carry more than one passenger if one of them is an experienced driver: authorised
-- to drive the novice's class, for at least 4 years under a licence other than a provisional one. The baseline's
-- `May I carry these passengers` is run for a type 1A novice (0 months) on the day r 11 began, carrying two passengers
-- who are not family and not carried for work, the most experienced of them me: its answer turns on my years alone.
@export Am I an experienced driver, so that a new driver in their first 6 months may carry more than one passenger when I ride with them (Regulations r 11(3)(a), (4))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `years I have held a non-provisional licence for the new driver's class` IS A NUMBER @desc Years (adding up separate periods) you have held an Australian driver licence other than a provisional one, or an equivalent foreign authorisation, for the class of vehicle the new driver drives (0 if you hold none)
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Am I an experienced driver for a new driver's passenger limit` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I supervise a learner driver, or ride with a new driver` THEN
        `yes if` (`May I carry these passengers` `the day the passenger restriction came into operation` 0
                    (`My passengers` 2 `years I have held a non-provisional licence for the new driver's class` FALSE FALSE))
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`
